          "body": "I think DJB is correct here:\r\n\r\nhttps://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ipr-wg/AKwQUKZ1dzaLgwaIqLaqPIrWmIE/\r\n\r\nSection 3 is non-normative.  So, this draft changes Section 5.3c. This distinction is why we get one person claiming there's no change, and another person claiming it's really aggressive.  I'm in the middle: it is a change, but the IETF is not required to provide an official email footer. If you really need it, you can write an I-D easily enough.\r\n\r\nThis is why I bothered to write this one in the first place. While it doesn't seem DJB agrees with the change, I do agree with his read here. (I'll click the buttons if you want, but imho there needs to be more clarity on this issue)",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-27T04:09:02Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-07-27T05:04:07Z"
        },
        {
          "author": "becarpenter",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "body": "Let me try one more bit of wordsmithing (but remember that BCP14 terminology is not a necessity).",
          "createdAt": "2026-07-27T05:10:08Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-07-27T05:10:08Z"
        }
